The graph shows a curve $y = f(x)$ with a tangent line drawn at $(2, 5)$ passing through $(0, 1)$ and $(4, 9)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (5.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,5.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5} {\draw (\x,0) -- (\x,-0.12); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.12) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y/\val in {1/2,2/4,3/6,4/8,5/10} {\draw (-0.12,\y) -- (0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.12,\y) {$\val$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:4.2,smooth,variable=\x] plot (\x, {0.15*\x*\x + 0.4*\x + 1.1}) node[above left] {$y=f(x)$};
\draw[thick,dashed,red] (0,0.5) -- (4.5,5.0);
\fill (2,2.5) circle (2.5pt) node[above left] {$(2,5)$};
\fill (0,0.5) circle (2.5pt) node[below right] {$(0,1)$};
\fill (4,4.5) circle (2.5pt) node[below right] {$(4,9)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What is the estimated instantaneous rate of change $f'(2)$?

Water drains from a tank.
The volume $V$ (litres) after $t$ minutes is plotted, and the tangent line at $t = 4\text{ min}$ passes through $(0, 60)$ and $(8, 12)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (5.5,0) node[right] {$t$};
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,5.5) node[above] {$V$};
\foreach \x/\val in {1/2,2/4,3/6,4/8,5/10} {\draw (\x,0) -- (\x,-0.12); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.12) {$\val$};}
\foreach \y/\val in {1/20,2/40,3/60,4/80,5/100} {\draw (-0.12,\y) -- (0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.12,\y) {$\val$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:5.2,smooth,variable=\x] plot (\x, {0.6 + 3.262*exp(-0.5*\x)}) node[above right] {$V(t)$};
\draw[thick,dashed,red] (0,3.0) -- (4,0.6);
\fill (2,1.8) circle (2.5pt) node[above right] {$(4,36)$};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.3,2.75) {Volume (L)};
\node[below] at (2.7,-0.9) {Time (min)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What is the estimated instantaneous rate of change of the volume at $t = 4\text{ minutes}$?

The graph shows $y=f(x)$ with a tangent drawn at $x=2$. What is the estimated value of $f'(2)$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.85]
\draw[gray!30,very thin] (0,0) grid (4,5);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(4.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,5.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4} {\draw (\x,0)--(\x,-0.1) node[below] {$\x$};}
\foreach \y/\v in {1/5,2/10,3/15,4/20,5/25} {\draw (0,\y)--(-0.1,\y) node[left] {$\v$};}
\node[below left] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:4,samples=60] plot (\x,{0.15*(\x-2)^2+\x+0.4});
\draw[thick,dashed,red] (0,0.4)--(4,4.4);
\fill (2,2.4) circle (2.5pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The graph shows $y=f(x)$ with a tangent at $P(3,7)$ passing through $(1,1)$ and $(5,13)$. What is the estimated instantaneous rate of change at $x=3$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.85]
\draw[gray!30,very thin] (0,0) grid (5,5);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(5.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,5.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5} {\draw (\x,0)--(\x,-0.1) node[below] {$\x$};}
\foreach \y/\v in {1/3,2/6,3/9,4/12,5/15} {\draw (0,\y)--(-0.1,\y) node[left] {$\v$};}
\node[below left] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0.5:5,samples=60] plot (\x,{0.1*(\x-3)^2+\x-2/3});
\draw[thick,dashed,red] (0.7,0.7-2/3)--(5,13/3);
\fill (3,7/3) circle (2.5pt) node[above left] {$P$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A runner's distance–time graph has a tangent drawn at $t = 6\text{ s}$ that passes through $(3, 15)$ and $(9, 63)$, where distance is in metres.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.85]
\draw[gray!30,very thin] (0,0) grid (5,5);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(5.5,0) node[right] {$t\text{ (s)}$};
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,5.5) node[above] {$d\text{ (m)}$};
\foreach \x/\v in {1/2,2/4,3/6,4/8,5/10} {\draw (\x,0)--(\x,-0.1) node[below] {$\v$};}
\foreach \y/\v in {1/15,2/30,3/45,4/60,5/75} {\draw (0,\y)--(-0.1,\y) node[left] {$\v$};}
\node[below left] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:5,samples=60] plot (\x,{(4/45)*\x*\x+(8/15)*\x+0.2});
\draw[thick,dashed,red] (0.6,0.04)--(5,71/15);
\fill (3,2.6) circle (2.5pt) node[above left] {$(6,39)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What is the runner's estimated instantaneous speed at $t = 6\text{ seconds}$?

The graph shows a curve $y = f(x)$ with a tangent line at $(2, 3)$ passing through $(0, -5)$ and $(3, 7)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[->] (-1,0) -- (5.0,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3) -- (0,4.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4} {\draw (\x,0) -- (\x,-0.12); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.12) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y/\val in {-2/-4,1/2,2/4,3/6,4/8} {\draw (-0.12,\y) -- (0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.12,\y) {$\val$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:3.2,smooth,variable=\x] plot (\x, {0.3*\x*\x + 0.8*\x - 1.3}) node[above left] {$y=f(x)$};
\draw[thick,dashed,red] (0.5,-1.5) -- (3.5,4.5);
\fill (2,1.5) circle (2.5pt) node[below right] {$(2,3)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the estimated derivative $f'(2)$.

A bamboo plant's height $H$ in centimetres over $t$ days is plotted on a graph.
The tangent line at $t = 5\text{ days}$ passes through $(2, 6)$ and $(8, 24)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.85]
\draw[gray!30,very thin] (0,0) grid (5,5);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(5.5,0) node[right] {$t\text{ (days)}$};
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,5.5) node[above] {$H\text{ (cm)}$};
\foreach \x/\v in {1/2,2/4,3/6,4/8,5/10} {\draw (\x,0)--(\x,-0.1) node[below] {$\v$};}
\foreach \y/\v in {1/6,2/12,3/18,4/24,5/30} {\draw (0,\y)--(-0.1,\y) node[left] {$\v$};}
\node[below left] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:4.5,samples=60] plot (\x,{0.1*(\x-2.5)^2+\x});
\draw[thick,dashed,red] (0,0)--(5,5);
\fill (2.5,2.5) circle (2.5pt) node[above left] {$(5,15)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What is the estimated instantaneous growth rate at $t = 5\text{ days}$?

The graph of $y=f(x)$ shows a tangent line drawn at $(2,7)$ passing through $(0,1)$ and $(4,13)$. What is the estimated instantaneous rate of change $f'(2)$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.85]
\draw[gray!30,very thin] (0,0) grid (5,5);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(5.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,5.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5} {\draw (\x,0)--(\x,-0.1) node[below] {$\x$};}
\foreach \y/\v in {1/3,2/6,3/9,4/12,5/15} {\draw (0,\y)--(-0.1,\y) node[left] {$\v$};}
\node[below left] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:4,samples=60] plot (\x,{0.1*(\x-2)^2+\x+1/3});
\draw[thick,dashed,red] (0,1/3)--(4.5,4.5+1/3);
\fill (2,7/3) circle (2.5pt) node[above left] {$(2,7)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
